@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Garage washing visual refinement
+
+Owner request, 2026-10-14: improve the first washing animation toward the AAA target, followed by a specific rejection of the foam style. GWP01: a believable soft wash mitt and material finish. GWP02: visually richer connected foam. GWP03: natural scrubbing, water and runoff. GWP04: actual surface seating, bounded resources and preserved local cleaning/input/condition. GWA01-GWA03, CW13/CW15/CW16, V06/G01/R01/Q01 remain applicable.
+
+The rectangular sponge is now an original rounded microfiber mitt with a thumb, closed nap tufts and an actual closed ribbed cuff with a stitched finish. Filtered fabric shading preserves a matte, soft appearance. The mitt gently compresses and follows the swipe direction; rapid reversals retain its orientation rather than flipping it. A held stroke uses a smaller, slower oval scrub. Water has smooth translucent dielectric droplets, a restrained Fresnel rim and gravity-shaped elongation, with lower outward velocity.
+
+The owner's foam feedback is incorporated in the final version. It replaces separated speckled stamps and a flat blurred film with connected creamy froth, real raised small air pockets, irregular softened outlines and elongated overlapping streaks behind the mitt. The dense base avoids dark crater-like bubble holes. Tiny aeration is filtered at display scale; the rounded air pockets provide actual highlights and volume. Surface-projected gravity moves side-panel lather downward. Geometry and materials remain native and original, without a generated bitmap, external dependency or runtime service.
+
+The original 24 lather / 32 water pools, one lazily created effect and four geometry draws per receiving view remain. Three immutable mitt/cuff/lather meshes are shared across the five cars; water reuses a smooth sphere in its fixed MultiMesh. The existing two reflection views include the effect, with no new camera or colour capture. Lather reads the current view's opaque depth once to suppress unsupported edges and floating halos. Reconstruction follows [Godot's depth documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/advanced_postprocessing.html); per-instance lifetime data follows [Godot's spatial shader API](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/spatial_shader.html). No extra shadow caster, car material/mesh change, wash-rate change, condition schema/save change, camera change or canonical simulation change is introduced. Visual cleanup now owns a shallow copy of the hit descriptor so it cannot clear the caller's data.
+
+Actual evidence: [before/after](evidence/garage-wash-polish-2026-10-14/gl_compatibility/after/before-after.png), [final Compatibility animation](evidence/garage-wash-polish-2026-10-14/gl_compatibility/after/washing-animation.webp), [final Mobile animation](evidence/garage-wash-polish-2026-10-14/mobile/after/washing-animation.webp), [phone-sized hood view](evidence/garage-wash-polish-2026-10-14/gl_compatibility/after/quality/hood-960.png) and [foam alone on actual paint](evidence/garage-wash-polish-2026-10-14/gl_compatibility/after/quality/lather-only.png). Each animation uses 72 actual native renders, resized to 960x540 for review; production updates are stepped at 30 Hz. This is not a frame-rate measurement. Earlier foam attempts and their sources are retained in `foam-iteration/`. The initial effect is compiled from its saved source only by the explicit test-only `--before-effect` argument. Concurrent LP/room revisions are preserved; the photos use the same camera/input fixture rather than claiming all background assets stayed hash-identical between runs.
+
+Actual commands use the pinned `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` through `scripts/dev.ps1`, isolated APPDATA under `build/garage-wash-polish-user` and separate local test records:
+
+```powershell
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_polish.ps1 -Before
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_polish.ps1
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_polish.ps1 -Renderer mobile
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_polish.ps1 -Check test_garage_wash_polish
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_polish.ps1 -Check test_garage_wash_polish -Renderer mobile
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_polish.ps1 -Check test_car_wash
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_polish.ps1 -Check test_car_wash -Renderer mobile
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build/run_garage_wash_polish.ps1 -Check test_script_parse -Headless
+./.tools/review/Scripts/python.exe build/encode_garage_wash_polish.py
+python build/checkpoint_garage_wash_polish.py
+```
+
+Final passes: visual/surface/reversal checks **197 Compatibility + 197 Mobile**, all-car animation/input/local-saving checks **139 + 139**, original washing/lifecycle/real-app/paint-pixel checks **1,402 + 1,402**, and **760-script parse**, all zero failures. The rendered-face assertion confirms the air-pocket geometry actually appears in the indexed draw. Original paint/camera/kits/condition and pool identities remain; release/navigation/cancel/hide/teardown restore feedback. The original dirty-to-clean blue-paint assertion remains with transient feedback hidden for that comparison.
+
+Exact-pixel controls remain. Ending washing restores the original native render exactly. Unsupported lather contributes zero pixels against an otherwise identical native pass with only its instance opacity set to zero. The first Mobile comparison used an opaque-only baseline and exposed one-level whole-image rounding when the depth-reading transparent pass was present, including far outside the foam. The corrected clipping control retains that same pass; no colour tolerance or relaxed assertion is used. Initial cold target/sky work is settled before capturing the original image. Earlier failure images/logs are retained in the evidence, not counted as passes.
+
+Native aggregate render work across the original main1280x720 and two640x360 views goes from685518 to796686 visible triangles and adds10 visible draws in this pose; ending restores the exact idle counts. Detailed foam therefore has a real render cost. Final shared RTX3090 measurements are in each renderer's `quality/render-work.json`; concurrent desktop load makes timings noisy and no speedup/phone-FPS claim is made. Pools, lifetime and per-view caps remain bounded; no hidden steady-state draws are added.
+
+Other initial issues: copying the contact by reference allowed reset to clear the diagnostic's hit descriptor; the final effect copies it and an ownership check passes. A concurrent records-menu/library interface temporarily blocked one Garage run; its later source revision passes without changes from this task. Indexed SurfaceTool geometry initially omitted appended air pockets; deindexing before append and reindexing afterward includes them, and the rendered-volume assertion is retained. Native Windows runs require the previously authorized certificate-store read. Attempt logs are under `attempts/`; scoped whitespace checking and the isolated two-commit checkpoint are recorded in `checkpoint.json`.
+
+Runtime files: `game/ui/garage_wash_effect.gd`, new `garage_wash_geometry.gd`, `garage_wash_cloth.gdshader`, `garage_wash_lather.gdshader`, `garage_wash_water.gdshader` (+UIDs). Tests: updated `test_garage_wash_animation.gd` (saved-baseline capture, actual hood path, normalized direction comparison with compression), new `test_garage_wash_polish.gd` (+UID). Runner, encoder and checkpoint procedure are in `build/`. Main branch/index and unrelated LP/room/vehicle work are preserved.
+
+Owner foam/style and physical-phone appearance, touch, first-contact shader preparation, frame-pacing and thermal acceptance remain. Manual review: wash the dark door and light hood, sweep rapidly in both directions, hold still, move off the body, rotate with two fingers/right mouse, release and reopen Care; confirm foam looks natural at the actual phone framing and cleaned areas persist. No physical-phone/attachment check, APK export/install/deployment, backend write, full Validate or physics merge was performed. The AAA target is not a certification of final owner/device quality.
